31
00:45:48.942 --> 00:45:51.942
I personally went to Iraq for days.

32
00:45:51.942 --> 00:45:53.942
To practically help people there.

33
00:45:53.942 --> 00:45:55.942
And to tell people about Jesus.

34
00:45:57.942 --> 00:45:59.942
We mainly worked with refugees.

35
00:45:59.942 --> 00:46:02.942
And helped them practically there.

36
00:46:02.942 --> 00:46:03.942
Distributed food.

37
00:46:03.942 --> 00:46:05.442
Listened to their stories.

38
00:46:05.442 --> 00:46:06.942
And looked at what they needed.

39
00:46:08.442 --> 00:46:10.942
And it was hard to see the pain there.

40
00:46:10.942 --> 00:46:12.942
To hear the stories of the people.

41
00:46:12.942 --> 00:46:14.942
They have really experienced terrible things.

42
00:46:15.942 --> 00:46:16.942
A lot of violence.

43
00:46:16.942 --> 00:46:18.942
There is a lot of racism there too.

44
00:46:18.942 --> 00:46:20.942
Among people themselves.

45
00:46:21.942 --> 00:46:23.942
It was very painful to see.

46
00:46:23.942 --> 00:46:25.942
But at the same time, it was so beautiful.

47
00:46:25.942 --> 00:46:28.942
There were so many people who had never heard of the Bible before.

48
00:46:28.942 --> 00:46:30.942
Never heard of Jesus.

49
00:46:30.942 --> 00:46:32.942
They asked, what is the Bible anyway?

50
00:46:32.942 --> 00:46:34.942
And that really broke my heart.

51
00:46:34.942 --> 00:46:36.942
But that those people were so hungry.

52
00:46:36.942 --> 00:46:38.942
That we could share the love of Jesus with them.

53
00:46:38.942 --> 00:46:40.942
That we could proclaim freedom.

54
00:46:41.942 --> 00:46:42.942
And...

55
00:46:42.942 --> 00:46:43.942
Yes...

56
00:46:43.942 --> 00:46:44.942
Just that Jesus loves them.

57
00:46:44.942 --> 00:46:46.942
That Jesus can bring them peace.

58
00:46:46.942 --> 00:46:49.942
That He can be their hope in such a hopeless situation.

59
00:46:49.942 --> 00:46:50.942
It was so beautiful.

60
00:46:50.942 --> 00:46:53.942
And there are so many people who wanted to know more about Jesus.

61
00:46:53.942 --> 00:46:55.942
Those who are reading the Bible now.

62
00:46:55.942 --> 00:46:56.942
And...

63
00:46:56.942 --> 00:46:58.942
Yes, the long-termers are going to take over now.

64
00:46:58.942 --> 00:47:01.942
And I truly believe that God is doing great things there.

65
00:47:01.942 --> 00:47:02.942
And also here.

66
00:47:02.942 --> 00:47:03.942
Just a quick question, okay?

67
00:47:03.942 --> 00:47:04.942
So...

68
00:47:05.942 --> 00:47:06.942
The...

69
00:47:07.942 --> 00:47:10.942
The suffering that these people have seen in Iraq.

70
00:47:10.942 --> 00:47:15.942
Are you still referring to the previous Gulf War?

71
00:47:15.942 --> 00:47:18.942
And the aftermath of that which continues in this country.

72
00:47:18.942 --> 00:47:19.942
What is...

73
00:47:19.942 --> 00:47:21.942
What does this country suffer from the most?

74
00:47:24.942 --> 00:47:27.942
Indeed, the war has had a large part in that.

75
00:47:27.942 --> 00:47:29.942
There is a lot that is broken in the country.

76
00:47:29.942 --> 00:47:32.942
People have seen a lot that they are still suffering from.

77
00:47:32.942 --> 00:47:34.942
But there are also many refugees.

78
00:47:34.942 --> 00:47:36.942
Mainly from Syria who are there.

79
00:47:36.942 --> 00:47:38.942
Who have simply experienced ISIS.

80
00:47:38.942 --> 00:47:40.942
Who have had to flee from their country.

81
00:47:40.942 --> 00:47:42.942
They are now living in a lot of poverty.

82
00:47:42.942 --> 00:47:44.942
And there is therefore a lot of pain from that.

83
00:47:44.942 --> 00:47:47.942
Because in which year was the last war in Iraq?

84
00:47:47.942 --> 00:47:49.942
Bram, you know that.

85
00:47:53.942 --> 00:47:54.942
Yes, it was...

86
00:47:55.942 --> 00:47:56.942
The war...

87
00:47:57.942 --> 00:48:00.942
Yes, you have to count presidents and then...

88
00:48:00.942 --> 00:48:01.942
But...

89
00:48:02.942 --> 00:48:03.942
Yes, that's why.

90
00:48:03.942 --> 00:48:04.942
And so...

91
00:48:04.942 --> 00:48:07.942
That overturn of Hussein.

92
00:48:07.942 --> 00:48:09.942
What I want to indicate is...

93
00:48:09.942 --> 00:48:11.942
Look at what a war does.

94
00:48:12.942 --> 00:48:15.942
There is not a war today and tomorrow we rebuild.

95
00:48:15.942 --> 00:48:18.942
This has repercussions for decades.

96
00:48:18.942 --> 00:48:19.942
And that is intense.

97
00:48:20.942 --> 00:48:21.942
And God says...

98
00:48:21.942 --> 00:48:22.942
In the Bible, God says...

99
00:48:22.942 --> 00:48:26.942
If you live in the grace and in the truth of the Father...

100
00:48:26.942 --> 00:48:30.942
Then you will be a blessing to the generations to come.

101
00:48:30.942 --> 00:48:32.942
Conversely, the Bible says.

102
00:48:32.942 --> 00:48:35.942
If you live in the shame of darkness...

103
00:48:35.942 --> 00:48:39.942
Then there will be shame and curse even to later generations.

104
00:48:39.942 --> 00:48:40.942
And this is what you look over.

105
00:48:40.942 --> 00:48:42.942
And I find it so cool...

106
00:48:42.942 --> 00:48:44.942
That we as a church may be a church...

107
00:48:44.942 --> 00:48:47.942
Where Nigaya grew up in this church...

108
00:48:47.942 --> 00:48:49.942
Someone who has such a heart for God...

109
00:48:49.942 --> 00:48:50.942
That she goes out into the world.

110
00:48:50.942 --> 00:48:52.942
Not staying here.

111
00:48:52.942 --> 00:48:53.942
Not remaining within the four walls.

112
00:48:53.942 --> 00:48:56.942
You must do what God calls you to do.

113
00:48:56.942 --> 00:48:57.942
To do what you need to do.

114
00:48:57.942 --> 00:48:59.942
And I find it super cool.

115
00:49:03.942 --> 00:49:04.942
Yes.

116
00:49:06.942 --> 00:49:11.942
God has also done a lot of miracles while we were there.

117
00:49:11.942 --> 00:49:14.942
We saw a lot of diseases.

118
00:49:14.942 --> 00:49:17.942
The healthcare system there is really not good at all.

119
00:49:17.942 --> 00:49:22.942
But we were able to ask many people if we could pray for them.

120
00:49:22.942 --> 00:49:25.942
I also saw very great faith in people who immediately said...

121
00:49:25.942 --> 00:49:27.942
Okay, when you pray, we believe that we will be healed.

122
00:49:27.942 --> 00:49:28.942
We saw that too.

123
00:49:28.942 --> 00:49:30.942
They were small things like headaches.

124
00:49:30.942 --> 00:49:33.942
But also people whose ears were opened...

125
00:49:33.942 --> 00:49:36.942
Wonderful, someone’s back disappeared.

126
00:49:36.942 --> 00:49:38.942
So God has really done great miracles there.

127
00:49:38.942 --> 00:49:39.942
Hallelujah.

128
00:49:39.942 --> 00:49:41.942
Great.

129
00:49:41.942 --> 00:49:42.942
Thanks Micaiah.

130
00:49:42.942 --> 00:49:43.942
Super thanks.

131
00:49:43.942 --> 00:49:44.942
Super thanks.

132
00:49:45.942 --> 00:49:46.942
Great.

133
00:49:46.942 --> 00:49:47.942
Hallelujah.

134
00:49:47.942 --> 00:49:48.942
Hallelujah.

135
00:49:49.942 --> 00:49:51.942
