138
00:50:04.942 --> 00:50:06.942
Proud dad.

139
00:50:06.942 --> 00:50:08.942
But I am also proud of you all.

140
00:50:08.942 --> 00:50:09.942
I was just standing there.

141
00:50:09.942 --> 00:50:11.942
During the worship still.

142
00:50:11.942 --> 00:50:15.942
And I saw how we were all worshiping God together.

143
00:50:15.942 --> 00:50:17.942
That is so great to see.

144
00:50:17.942 --> 00:50:19.942
Thank you for loving Jesus.

145
00:50:19.942 --> 00:50:21.942
That you worship him.

146
00:50:21.942 --> 00:50:23.942
That is completely worth it.

147
00:50:23.942 --> 00:50:25.942
My text can be on the screen.

148
00:50:26.942 --> 00:50:28.942
We will read together.

149
00:50:28.942 --> 00:50:31.942
1 Timothy 5, verse 17.

150
00:50:32.942 --> 00:50:38.942
Tell the people who are rich in this world not to be proud.

151
00:50:38.942 --> 00:50:42.942
Also that they should not trust in their riches.

152
00:50:42.942 --> 00:50:46.942
They can easily lose that wealth again.

153
00:50:46.942 --> 00:50:50.942
But they must trust in the living God in everything.

154
00:50:50.942 --> 00:50:57.942
He gives them everything abundantly to enjoy and to do good things with.

155
00:50:57.942 --> 00:51:02.942
The intention is that they are generous and share much of their wealth.

156
00:51:02.942 --> 00:51:06.942
In this way, they will store up for themselves a treasure.

157
00:51:06.942 --> 00:51:09.942
The assurance of a good future.

158
00:51:09.942 --> 00:51:12.942
For they will receive eternal life.

159
00:51:12.942 --> 00:51:15.942
And then back to verse 17.

160
00:51:15.942 --> 00:51:18.942
It is about rich people.

161
00:51:18.942 --> 00:51:22.942
So now you can say, that is a nice level applicable to me.

162
00:51:22.942 --> 00:51:24.942
For I am not that rich.

163
00:51:24.942 --> 00:51:30.942
But I chose this verse because of the aspect of trust that you see here.

164
00:51:32.942 --> 00:51:38.942
It says here, you should not trust in your riches, but you should trust in God.

165
00:51:38.942 --> 00:51:43.942
For riches are unreliable and God is completely trustworthy.

166
00:51:43.942 --> 00:51:48.942
And you can be rich and have a lot of money and then think, okay, now I am safe.

167
00:51:48.942 --> 00:51:52.942
We are all looking for safety in this world.

168
00:51:52.942 --> 00:51:53.942
For certainty.

169
00:51:53.942 --> 00:51:59.942
That you know what it will look like in a week or in a year or in ten years in your life.

170
00:51:59.942 --> 00:52:03.942
That your life is stable and safe and that you are doing well.

171
00:52:03.942 --> 00:52:05.942
That is what we are all looking for.

172
00:52:05.942 --> 00:52:08.942
And many people seek money in that.

173
00:52:08.942 --> 00:52:10.942
And you don't even have to be rich for that.

174
00:52:10.942 --> 00:52:12.942
You might also be struggling with this.

175
00:52:12.942 --> 00:52:16.942
Your job, your income, or maybe even your benefits.

176
00:52:16.942 --> 00:52:23.942
But you may have arranged your finances in such a way that you think, well, it's going okay or it's going well.

177
00:52:23.942 --> 00:52:26.942
And I feel safe for the future.

178
00:52:28.942 --> 00:52:30.942
And that is risky.

179
00:52:30.942 --> 00:52:35.942
For it is much better to trust in God.

180
00:52:35.942 --> 00:52:37.942
To build your life with God.

181
00:52:37.942 --> 00:52:42.942
For even if you manage to ensure that you always have it good here on earth.

182
00:52:43.942 --> 00:52:45.942
What does eternity mean then?

183
00:52:45.942 --> 00:52:48.942
What happens when you eventually die?

184
00:52:50.942 --> 00:52:53.942
If you build your life on God, then it will truly go well.

185
00:52:53.942 --> 00:52:58.942
Both here and in heaven.

186
00:52:58.942 --> 00:53:01.942
And you also see what God's heart is in this.

187
00:53:02.942 --> 00:53:05.942
He gives abundantly.

188
00:53:05.942 --> 00:53:11.942
So more than what is strictly necessary to enjoy and to do good things with.

189
00:53:11.942 --> 00:53:13.942
And that is truly God's heart.

190
00:53:13.942 --> 00:53:17.942
God does not want us to struggle here on earth.

191
00:53:17.942 --> 00:53:18.942
That we have it difficult.

192
00:53:18.942 --> 00:53:21.942
Not with our money or our security either.

193
00:53:21.942 --> 00:53:26.942
He just wants us to be well and to enjoy life as well.

194
00:53:26.942 --> 00:53:30.942
But He also wants us not to live just for ourselves.

195
00:53:30.942 --> 00:53:33.942
But that we also live for the world around us.

196
00:53:33.942 --> 00:53:35.942
Doing good things with our money.

197
00:53:35.942 --> 00:53:37.942
So I want to encourage you.

198
00:53:37.942 --> 00:53:40.942
Do not build your security only on money.

199
00:53:40.942 --> 00:53:42.942
And do not keep it just for yourself.

200
00:53:42.942 --> 00:53:44.942
But do it God's way.

201
00:53:44.942 --> 00:53:46.942
And be generous.

202
00:53:47.942 --> 00:53:57.942
If you've been coming to the church for a while, then you've probably noticed that we do a collection talk every week like now.

203
00:53:57.942 --> 00:53:59.942
And talking about money.

204
00:53:59.942 --> 00:54:01.942
Why do we do that?

205
00:54:01.942 --> 00:54:04.942
Because we are after as much money as possible?

206
00:54:04.942 --> 00:54:06.942
No, not at all.

207
00:54:06.942 --> 00:54:09.942
Because we want to put you under pressure.

208
00:54:09.942 --> 00:54:16.942
Or if we just keep repeating it long enough and more and more, you'll eventually fall for it and give more.

209
00:54:16.942 --> 00:54:18.942
That is totally not our intention.

210
00:54:20.942 --> 00:54:24.942
It's comparable to communion.

211
00:54:24.942 --> 00:54:29.942
Last week I explained that you shouldn't just take communion carelessly.

212
00:54:30.942 --> 00:54:36.942
But you should take communion when you choose to build your life on Jesus.

213
00:54:36.942 --> 00:54:38.942
To want to live with Him.

214
00:54:38.942 --> 00:54:45.942
And that's why it's so easy when those trays go around to also take it and partake.

215
00:54:45.942 --> 00:54:48.942
Because everyone does it and it comes by.

216
00:54:48.942 --> 00:54:54.942
In the past, we used to have baskets that went around where you could throw in the collections.

217
00:54:54.942 --> 00:54:56.942
Where you could throw in some money.

218
00:54:57.942 --> 00:55:03.942
Then it might also be like, okay, it comes by, I'll throw in a little too.

219
00:55:03.942 --> 00:55:07.942
And actually, it's nice that those baskets don't come around anymore.

220
00:55:07.942 --> 00:55:13.942
Because it makes no sense if you just throw in something casually.

221
00:55:13.942 --> 00:55:17.942
Just as it makes no sense to take communion casually.

222
00:55:18.942 --> 00:55:27.942
It is important that you do it out of love for Jesus, out of trust in Him, and out of a desire to build His kingdom.

223
00:55:27.942 --> 00:55:31.942
That you dedicate your life and that you invest your money.

224
00:55:31.942 --> 00:55:34.942
So think about that.

225
00:55:34.942 --> 00:55:40.942
Do not do it carelessly, do not do it because you have to or because everyone else is doing it.

226
00:55:40.942 --> 00:55:42.942
But do it out of love for Jesus.

227
00:55:42.942 --> 00:55:48.942
And if you are perhaps arranging your banking matters this week, talk to God about it again.

228
00:55:48.942 --> 00:55:52.942
Lord, I love you, I want to build your kingdom, I trust you.

229
00:55:52.942 --> 00:55:54.942
And then give, therefore.

